**Headline:** `^:slow` is only honoured by the JVM lane. Node (`:node-test`) and Dart (`cljd test`) have no filter, and 11 of the slow-tagged tests are unguarded `.cljc`, so both lanes still pay for them in full (about 250 s at JVM speed). Shrinking those tests is the main lever for Node and Dart; the default JVM lane has little pure redundancy left.

Seconds are from the JVM profile. "JVM default" is the saving in `bb test:clj`, "JVM slow" in `bb test:slow`. Node and Dart are unmeasured: the figure is the JVM-speed equivalent, and "—" means the test does not run there (`.clj`). Nothing was run for this audit.

